---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_449",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 449,
  "text": "[[2011.6]] <b>367₂.  De motu corporis DE MOTU CORPORIS </p>\n<p> [[2011.7]] <b>Corpus in Motu est</b>, quod est causa efficiens proxima cur pars quaelibet ipsius\n[[2011.8]] situm cum aliis corporibus mutet; alioqui dicitur <b>Quiescere</b>. </p>\n<p> [[2011.9]] Consideremus duo haec corpora, Solem et Tellurem, quae cum inter se distantias\n[[2011.10]] mutent, adeoque et situm, dicimus quidem aliquem adesse motum, sed non ideo dicere\n[[2011.11]] possumus utrum eorum moveatur aut quiescat, et an fortasse ambo moveantur, sed si\n[[2011.12]] sciamus quodnam causa proxima sit mutati situs, ei motum tribuemus; verbi gratia si\n[[2011.13]] telluri quaedam intelligentia inesset, quae illam circumageret; aut si paulo ante mota\n[[2011.14]] fuisse ponatur, quia motus semel positus sine ratione non desinit; aut si in fluido tellurem\n[[2011.15]] ambiente quaedam contingerent, quae ex vi quadam agendi telluris in motu existentis\n[[2011.16]] consequantur, aliter autem per causam aliquam explicari non possint, nempe si aether\n[[2012.1]] circumjectus ita a tellure recedat, uti ab ea rejici deberet, si ipsa moveretur, utique\n[[2012.2]] constabit tellurem moveri, nam aliter motus adeo varii in fluido ambiente ad unam\n[[2012.3]] causam revocari non possent. Quodsi nihil tale contingeret in sole, sola tellus foret in\n[[2012.4]] motu. Sin contingerent et in tellure et in sole, utrique motus attribuendus esset, et uterque\n[[2012.5]] pro parte ad mutationem situs contribuet. </p>\n<p> [[2012.6]] Partium autem mentionem in definitione ideo feci, quia si corpus circa proprium\n[[2012.7]] axem tantummodo moveatur, dici non potest ipsum mutare situm cum aliis, licet quaelibet\n[[2012.8]] ejus pars situm cum aliis mutet. Si chorda aliqua utrinque aequaliter tendatur, [<i>bricht\n[[2012.9]] ab</i>]\n [[2012.10]] <petit> </p>\n<p> [[2012.11]] <i>Die folgenden vier Absätze in Kleindruck stellen vier weiterführende Ansätze dar, die Leibniz nacheinander\n[[2012.12]] verworfen und im folgenden Stück wieder aufgegriffen hat</i>: </p>\n<p> [[2012.14]] Si vero tria sint corpora mutatio situs notari potest.\n[[2012.15]] Exempli causa ponamus tria esse corpora <i>a, b, c</i>, et per <i>a,\n[[2012.16]] b</i> transeat circulus cujus centrum sit <i>c</i> in quo sit spectator,\n[[2012.17]] et ponamus ipsa <i>a, b</i> distantiam quidem retinere a spectatore,\n[[2012.18]] sed mutare distantiam inter se, exempli causa <i>a</i>\n[[2012.19]] transire ex loco <i>1a</i> in locum <i>2a</i>, ipsis <i>b</i> et <i>c</i> immotis,\n[[2012.20]] utique notare potest spectator angulum <i>2acb</i> esse majorem\n[[2012.21]] quam <i>1acb</i>, sed si duo tantum essent corpora, ut si spectator\n[[2012.22]] esset in <i>b</i>, et corpus <i>a</i> moveretur, utique is qui esset\n[[2012.23]] in <i>b</i> non posset judicare [<i>bricht ab</i>] </p>\n<p> [[2012.24]] Si visibile consideretur instar puncti, et spectator quoque\n[[2012.25]] velut in puncto collocatus, sintque duo tantum puncta\n[[2012.26]] in quorum alterutro sit spectator, non poterit notare situs\n[[2012.27]] mutationem quae inter haec duo puncta contingat. Poterit vero eam notare, si punctum adhuc unum praeterea\n[[2012.28]] assumatur, et mutatio [<i>bricht ab</i>] </p>\n<p> [[2013.1]] Si duo tantum sint puncta in rerum natura, eaque situm mutare intelligantur, hoc non poterit notari; quia\n[[2013.2]] distantia est magnitudo intervalli, magnitudo autem sola comparatione intelligi potest. </p>\n<p> [[2013.3]] Si duo tantum ponantur [<i>bricht ab</i>] </petit> </p>\n",
  "number": "367₂.",
  "title": "De motu corporis",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:367₂. De motu corporis DE MOTU CORPORIS Corpus in Motu est, quod est causa efficiens proxima cur pars quaelibet ipsius situm cum aliis corporibus mutet; alioqui dicitur Quiescere. Consideremus duo haec corpora, Solem et Tellurem, quae cum inter se distantias mutent, adeoque et situm, dicimus quidem ...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>